      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "Pretty moderate maiden where IAMTHEDEVILSELBOW (4) will find this easier than the provincial's last time. Has shown enough to go close in this line-up. GRADIVUS (6) is a Victorian who was safely held over 1200m fresh and looks suited by the extra ground. Fitter and has upside having started only twice. HASTA LA SILVER (3) is also a two-start maiden and ran a much better race at second outing on heavy ground at Naracoorte. Likely improver who can get off the mark this time. KARMA QUEEN (7) has had quite a few chances but shows some ability and kept coming last time on the dirt at Port Augusta. Has the claim and looks a leading chance. CAESOUR'S TOMB (2) wasn't far away at the provincials last time and rates well on that run.",
